  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I'm well, thanks.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.41,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_25"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "My son has dyslexia and he's started saying he hates books. What can I do?",
   "est_sec": 4.75,
   "gap_before": 0.55,
   "block": "books.dlg14",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "That must be hard to hear. Audiobooks are a great way to keep him loving stories while reading gets easier.",
   "est_sec": 6.3,
   "gap_before": 0.33,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg14"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Isn't that kind of giving up on reading, though?",
   "est_sec": 2.89,
   "gap_before": 0.93,
   "block": "books.dlg14",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "No, it's a different road to the same place. Listening builds vocabulary and imagination. Many kids do both, listening and following along in the printed book.",
   "est_sec": 8.16,
   "gap_before": 0.73,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg14"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "His teacher mentioned special fonts. Do those actually help?",
   "est_sec": 2.89,
   "gap_before": 1.65,
   "block": "books.dlg14",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Some kids find them easier, some don't notice a difference. It's worth a try, along with bigger spacing between lines.",
   "est_sec": 6.3,
   "gap_before": 1.02,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg14"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "He loves dinosaurs. Like, obsessed.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 1.51,
   "block": "books.dlg14",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Then use that. Short nonfiction books about dinosaurs with big pictures can make reading feel like his thing again.",
   "est_sec": 5.99,
   "gap_before": 0.43,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg14"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Thank you. I've been",
